</span></div>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.29301v1/fig_hierarchy_rhombus.png" id="A4.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:685/635;" width="685" height="635" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure S4</span>: </span><span id="A4.F4.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">We demonstrate a case where <span id="A4.F4.6.1" class="ltx_text">Hierarchical-Consistency</span> chooses the correct warp but <span id="A4.F4.6.2" class="ltx_text">Majority-Consensus</span> fails by selecting a more restrictive warp.
